WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.537
This is where the
stand-ins earn their keep.

2
00:00:02.537 --> 00:00:06.688
The creation steps are fine, and
the code keeps them as its model.

3
00:00:06.688 --> 00:00:10.696
But the root key check uses a
command that returns the key itself,

4
00:00:10.696 --> 00:00:15.838
the secret every managed password comes
from, so the code reads only its start time.

5
00:00:15.838 --> 00:00:19.751
The backdated key is meant for
a test lab, not production.

6
00:00:19.751 --> 00:00:22.977
And one step sets the migration
state with a parameter

7
00:00:22.977 --> 00:00:26.275
the command simply doesn't
have, so as published it fails.

8
00:00:26.275 --> 00:00:28.671
Placeholder names that change from step to

9
00:00:28.671 --> 00:00:31.250
step are replaced by
names from reviewed data.
